# Apex bounce: front-door now owns `aquilla.app/` (apps/front-door/ is
# claim-routed), but the Pages-level rule stays as defense-in-depth in
# case the front-door worker is ever unbound.
/    /projects/    302

# Bare-slug → trailing-slash redirects. Workers Routes claims patterns
# like `aquilla.app/<slug>/*`, which match `/<slug>/foo` but NOT bare
# `/<slug>` (no trailing slash). Without these rules, requests for
# `/login`, `/projects`, etc. fall through to Pages, hit the SPA
# fallback below, render the workspace SPA's index.html, and the page
# blanks because no route matches `/login` inside the workspace router.
# Hard-coded list — adding an app means adding a line here AND a
# wrangler.toml route claim.
/login    /login/    301
/signup   /signup/   301
/reset    /reset/    301
/projects /projects/ 301
/import   /import/   301
/export   /export/   301
/migrate  /migrate/  301
/billing  /billing/  301
/org      /org/      301

# SPA fallback for the workspace bundle's apex routes (/project/:id,
# /debug, /settings/org, …). Matches everything not already redirected
# above.
/*    /index.html   200
